# Build-context hygiene for the deployment images. Their build context is the
# repository root (see deployments/docker/compose.yml), so everything below
# must keep local state, secrets, other worktrees, and unreadable directories
# out of the context — a root-owned e2e directory otherwise fails the build
# with "permission denied" before a single instruction runs.
#
# The same file is mirrored as Dockerfile.<name>.dockerignore next to each
# Dockerfile so builds work no matter which ignore-file mechanism the builder
# honors; keep them in sync. apps/web stays in the context because
# Dockerfile.web builds the dashboard from the repo root (its sync-openapi
# step reads api/openapi/shift.yaml); the desktop client is the only part of
# apps/ the images never need.

.git
.github
.claude
.kilo

.shift
.e2e-hosted
.e2e-storage
shift
bin
dist
coverage
coverage.out
tmp
data
apps/desktop
docs
tests
integrations
scripts
node_modules
**/node_modules
**/.next
*.log
**/*.log
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/.DS_Store
